<figure class="diagram">
<div class="diagram__pair">
<div class="diagram__cell">
<svg viewBox="0 0 300 240" role="img" aria-labelledby="bridgeTitle bridgeDesc" class="diagram__svg">
<title id="bridgeTitle">The bridge model</title>
<desc id="bridgeDesc">Two separated circles joined by an application bridge, with the text's aim landing only on the original audience. The whole model is crossed out.</desc>
<text x="20" y="26" class="d-telos">Telos of the text</text>
<line x1="40" y1="34" x2="70" y2="86" class="d-telos-line" marker-end="url(#dArrowMarker)"/>
<circle cx="78" cy="128" r="46" class="d-ring"/>
<circle cx="222" cy="128" r="46" class="d-ring"/>
<text x="78" y="123" class="d-label">Original</text>
<text x="78" y="140" class="d-label">audience</text>
<text x="222" y="123" class="d-label">Contemporary</text>
<text x="222" y="140" class="d-label">audience</text>
<line x1="124" y1="128" x2="176" y2="128" class="d-bridge" marker-end="url(#dArrowThin)"/>
<text x="150" y="151" class="d-bridge-label">Application</text>
<text x="150" y="164" class="d-bridge-label">bridge</text>
<line x1="24" y1="52" x2="276" y2="212" class="d-reject"/>
<line x1="276" y1="52" x2="24" y2="212" class="d-reject"/>
</svg>
<figcaption class="diagram__cap"><span class="diagram__tag diagram__tag--no">How we&rsquo;re often taught</span>The bridge model: the text&rsquo;s aim lands back in the ancient world, and <em>you</em> must build a span to carry it across.</figcaption>
</div>
<div class="diagram__cell">
<svg viewBox="0 0 300 240" role="img" aria-labelledby="overlapTitle overlapDesc" class="diagram__svg">
<title id="overlapTitle">The overlap model</title>
<desc id="overlapDesc">Two heavily overlapping circles with the shared audience in the middle, and the text's aim landing directly on the overlap.</desc>
<text x="150" y="24" class="d-telos" text-anchor="middle">Telos of the text</text>
<line x1="140" y1="32" x2="132" y2="70" class="d-telos-line" marker-end="url(#dArrowMarker)"/>
<line x1="160" y1="32" x2="168" y2="70" class="d-telos-line" marker-end="url(#dArrowMarker)"/>
<circle cx="128" cy="140" r="64" class="d-ring"/>
<circle cx="172" cy="140" r="64" class="d-ring"/>
<text x="58" y="140" class="d-label">Original</text>
<text x="242" y="140" class="d-label">Contemporary</text>
<text x="150" y="136" class="d-label d-label--mid">Audience</text>
<text x="150" y="152" class="d-label d-label--mid">(shared)</text>
</svg>
<figcaption class="diagram__cap"><span class="diagram__tag diagram__tag--yes">A better way</span>The overlap model: the text&rsquo;s aim lands directly on the ground the two audiences share &mdash; you <em>recognize</em> where it points.</figcaption>
</div>
</div>
<svg width="0" height="0" aria-hidden="true" style="position:absolute"><defs><marker id="dArrowMarker" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M 0 1 L 9 5 L 0 9 z" class="d-arrowhead"/></marker><marker id="dArrowThin" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M 0 1 L 9 5 L 0 9 z" class="d-arrowhead-ink"/></marker></defs></svg>
</figure>
